#
# Aquantia atlantic-forwarding driver config
#

if AQFWD

config ATLFWD_FWD
       bool "Enable forwarding-engine API"
       default n
       help

         Enable the forwarding-engine API that provides direct hardware access
         for high-performance packet processing applications. This API allows
         user-space applications and kernel modules to bypass the standard
         network stack and directly interact with the hardware forwarding
         rings for zero-copy packet transmission and reception.

         The forwarding-engine API provides:
         - Direct ring buffer access for minimal latency packet processing
         - Hardware-accelerated packet forwarding capabilities
         - Custom packet classification and filtering
         - Integration with user-space networking frameworks
         - Support for specialized networking applications

         This feature is essential for applications that require maximum
         throughput and minimum latency, such as network function virtualization
         (NFV), software-defined networking (SDN), packet inspection, and
         high-frequency trading applications.

         If you are building a general-purpose system or don't need specialized
         packet forwarding capabilities, say N. Say Y only if you specifically
         need direct hardware access for high-performance networking applications.

config ATLFWD_FWD_RXBUF
       int
       prompt "Rx buffer space for forwarding engine's rings" if ATLFWD_FWD
       range 0 320
       default 160 if ATLFWD_FWD
       default 0
       help

         Amount of Rx buffer to reserve for the forwarding-engine
         rings. This sets the default value of the fwd_rx_buf_reserve
         module option.

         Value in kiB, 0 to 320, defaults to 160 if forwarding-engine
         API enabled, 0 otherwise.

config ATLFWD_FWD_TXBUF
       int
       prompt "Tx buffer space for forwarding engine's rings" if ATLFWD_FWD
       range 0 160
       default 80 if ATLFWD_FWD
       default 0
       help

         Amount of Tx buffer to reserve for the forwarding-engine
         rings. This sets the default value of the fwd_tx_buf_reserve
         module option.

         Value in kiB, 0 to 320, defaults to 80 if forwarding-engine
         API enabled, 0 otherwise.

config ATLFWD_FWD_NETLINK
        bool "Enable netlink control socket for forwarding engine"
        default y
        depends on ATLFWD_FWD
        help

          Expose forwarding engine APIs over the netlink socket.

endif
